<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul to approve 45 bln won small firm bond issues.</title>
<headline>Seoul to approve 45 bln won small firm bond issues.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities Supervisory Board said on Friday it plans to approve four small companies to issue bonds totalling 45 billion won to be sold exclusively to foreigners.  </p>
<p>The board said Hanmi Leasing Co and ALEX Computer would be allowed to issue 15 billion won worth of such bonds each.</p>
<p>DI Corp would be permitted to issue bonds worth five billion won and HS Electronics Corp 10 billion won, it said.</p>
<p>In January, South Korea allowed small and medium-sized companies to raise funds by selling non-guranteed bonds to foreigners.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
